Indra orders Rambhā to tempt Kauśika with desire and delusion --- Rambhā pleads fear of Viśvāmitra's terrible anger --- Indra reassures Rambhā and promises aid with Kāma beside her --- Rambhā assumes radiant beauty and tempts Viśvāmitra --- Viśvāmitra hears cuckoo song and gazes at Rambhā --- Viśvāmitra detects Indra's plot and curses Rambhā to stone for ten thousand years --- Rambhā becomes stone and Kāma departs from sage --- Viśvāmitra repents his anger and finds no peace